  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour.rs`: on an outside ring, the Arc entry does not run its vertical wall arc when the lead-in is `Lead::None`. The level descends by the grazing dive at the ring's start. A note names the stand-down once.\n- `crates/app/tests/contour_none_lead.rs`: new pins. Each test edits the contour through `EditOperationParams` and generates it, as the page's Apply does.\n- `docs/decisions/3132-contour-none-lead.md`: the decision record.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe report does not name the entry type. On `Milling-test.step`, only the Arc entry reproduces the symptom. Plunge, Ramp and Helix with both leads None already start the cut on the ring.\n\nWith both leads None, the Arc entry's wall arc lands on the seam itself. Its start is about 8.7 mm back along the seam's tangent. From above, that arc is a straight move into the seam. It has the same shape as the seeded 8 mm linear lead. An Arc lead changes the shape, and a Linear lead keeps it, as the report says.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, all in `contour_none_lead`:\n- `arc_entry_with_both_leads_none_starts_the_cut_on_the_ring`: Linear to None, Lead out None, zero extensions, zero overlap, Arc entry. The first XY cut is flat at the level and starts on the ring's closed seam. The post has no G18/G19.\n- `plunge_entry_with_both_leads_none_starts_the_cut_on_the_ring`: the same check for the Plunge entry.\n- `linear_and_arc_leads_keep_their_shapes`: Linear gives an 8 mm straight lead, and Arc gives an arc lead. A change back to None removes the lead.\n- `arc_entry_with_a_linear_lead_still_descends_on_its_arc`: the wall arc still runs when there is a lead.\n\nMutation checks on head `155793d04` (merged with upstream/main `8a6c6921b`):\n1. `no_lead_in` forced to `false` (the main behaviour): `arc_entry_with_both_leads_none_starts_the_cut_on_the_ring` fails at line 126. Restored: green.\n2. `no_lead_in` forced to `true` (the arc stands down for every lead): `arc_entry_with_a_linear_lead_still_descends_on_its_arc` fails at line 164. Restored: green.\n\nGate on head `155793d04`:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 27 steps, 0 failed, 4.6 min. The steps include `contour_none_lead`, `wall_arc_entry`, `arc_entry`, `vertical_arc_entry`, `entry_arc`, `solid_law_goldens` and the motion lib.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: green, 237 steps, 0 failed, 33.0 min. The lanes that ran are the reached `motion heavy` and `app heavy` lanes, in release with `--ignored`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The user's project `O4 Cam Plate master` is not available here. The fix follows the one reproduction on `Milling-test.step`. If the user's entry is not Arc, reopen the issue with the entry type.\n- The bore side (Side::Inside) Arc entry does not change. In a bore, the ramp, helix and arc are certified entries in bounded air. The decision file gives the reason.\n- With a tool that is not centre-cutting, an Arc entry, and no lead-in, the graze's centre-cutting refusal now applies. Its hint \"pick the Arc entry\" does not help in that case. A wording follow-up can name the lead.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #3120 changes `lead_fit.rs`, `lead_seam.rs` and `mod.rs`. This PR does not change those files, so there is no overlap.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Contour with both lead shapes set to None no longer keeps a straight entry at the seam: the Arc entry's wall arc stands down and the level dives at the ring's start (#3132).\n\nFixes #3132\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
